#: docs/index.md:37
#, python-brace-format
msgid "1. The work plan is where you say what you are doing. Not a chat message, not a comment — <a0>work items</a0>, a committed store any session or agent can read. Claim before you work so a sibling session does not pick up the same item; a work item that turns out not to be wanted is {code0}, with its reasons, never deleted."
msgstr ""

#: docs/index.md:50
msgid "2. Make your first folio. This repository is the platform; your content lives in its own. One command scaffolds it — the manifests, the declaration, the agent files and the link back here:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/index.md:61
msgid "3. Know which kind of thing you are writing. A document is structured prose; a paper is that plus the block kinds whose assertion is a formal claim, backed by Lean and typeset through LaTeX. The choice decides which blocks are legal and which gates run: <a0>Content types</a0>."
msgstr ""

#: docs/index.md:66
msgid "4. The rest of the documentation. <a0>All of it</a0> — the authoring guides, the architecture, the publication workflow, the generated schema and skill reference. Read it when you need it; the three steps above are the ones worth reading now."
msgstr ""

